    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup as the clear top play, boasting an 81.87 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against a right-handed pitcher, combined with a significant park factor and a premium leadoff spot, makes him the engine of the offense. Close behind is **Jacob Wilson**, whose 71.63 score is bolstered by a massive 17% SP skill advantage against a vulnerable arm, while **Heliot Ramos** and **Sam Antonacci** provide high-ceiling utility due to their aggressive baserunning profiles against slow deliveries, providing a critical boost in our pursuit of stolen base volume.\n\nPlatoon edges are dictating much of our decision-making today, particularly with **Miguel Vargas** and **Andy Pages** receiving elevated scores due to park factors and hitting order placement. **Josh Lowe** and **Kyle Tucker** remain in the mix despite the \"Lineup Pending\" designation, as their underlying efficiency against the pitching staff holds their value above the replacement threshold. The most difficult bench decision was opting to keep **Nasim Nunez** on the sidelines; while his speed is an asset, his projection dropped to 47.22 primarily due to a lower batting order slot and a high-efficiency holding pitcher suppressing his stolen base upside. We are proceeding with caution regarding the outfield spots for **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**, as these are predicated on assumed lineup positions; any downward shift in the order prior to first pitch will necessitate a final recalibration of our projected efficiency.",
